## Dead Ends
Pooling the selector numerator and denominator across gradient-accumulated microbatches would require retaining computation graphs or changing the shared trainer protocol. The minimal safe implementation rejects accumulation greater than one instead of adding that larger refactor.

## Hints for Future Agents
Do not raise draft_accumulation_steps for DFlash2 until auxiliary-loss numerators and denominators can be pooled once per optimizer step. The restriction is specific to the TorchSpec-defined selector objective. The D-PACE valid mask must enter before cumulative products; multiplying only the final weights allows masked suffix confidences to affect earlier tokens.

## Codebase Discoveries
The shared trainer backpropagates each microbatch loss immediately and divides it by accumulation_steps. This supports accumulation for fixed-normalization objectives but cannot produce a token-pooled auxiliary mean when eligible token counts differ. DFlash target layer IDs use zero-based decoder-layer indices and must be less than target_num_hidden_layers.

## Open Questions
A future shared loss protocol could return differentiable numerators plus detached counts and normalize them across all microbatches in one optimizer step. No CUDA or multi-rank runtime was available to validate that larger design.
